<card n:imported="components/feature-card.nijor" />

<body>
    <div class="main">
        <h1>Why use Nijor ?</h1>
        <div class="cards">
            <card title="Reusability" icon="reuse">
                Write your code in reausable components which can be reused multiple times, thus making your code look
                cleaner, easier to debug and more organized. Write components in *.nijor files.
            </card>
            <card title="Scoped CSS" icon="box">
                CSS inside your components are scoped which means that you don't need to think about your component's
                css affecting other components or vise-versa. You can write global styles in the style.css file.
            </card>
            <card title="Routing" icon="compass">
                A file-system based client-side router. Works automatically based on your file arrangement. No
                configuration required ; no extra code needed. Supports parameterized routing.
            </card>
            <card title="SSR Support" icon="deploy">
                SSR in Nijor works a little different than other frameworks. However, it doesn't effect SEO adversely.
            </card>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>

<style>
    .main{
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        flex-shrink: 0;
        padding: 0.5rem;
    }
    h1{
        flex-shrink: 0;
        margin: 1rem;
        text-align: center;
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: 35px;
        letter-spacing: 1px;
    }
    .cards {
        padding: 0.5rem;
        padding-top: 1rem;
        width: 100%;
        background-color: transparent;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: row;
        align-self: center;
        justify-content: space-evenly;
        flex-wrap: nowrap;
        flex-shrink: 0;
        align-content: center;
        overflow: hidden;
    }

    @media only screen and (max-width: 1200px) {
        .cards {
            flex-wrap: wrap;
        }
    }
</style>